      "writtenOn": "2017-02-02T17:43:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We shouldn\u0027t have this committed into the framework as the default value if it is a requirement for specific carriers. For example, as a user in the US, if I saw this on my device, I would have no idea what \"MM#X\" means.\n\nInstead, in values/strings.xml, we should include the generic string \"SIM not provisioned\" and then in the carrier specific values-mccXXX-mncXXX file you can override it with the message highlighted here for all carriers where this requirement applies.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4444,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 4444,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "50d7d211dc2124548e5f2efd5f6d8f760595b511",
